            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No, not really. They are for different things:\n- [`config.options.win_borders` is a shortcut for some of the keys of 'fillchar' option](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3ad46cdb7a51281e0024416023b56cf5c7909ae7/doc/mini-basics.txt#L193-L201). It defines borders between *normal* (i.e. split) windows.\n- The 'winborder' on Neovim>=0.11 option is for floating windows and is [already supported](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#version-01509000) across the whole 'mini.nvim'.",
